  "title": "Qt: InterfaceFrame: Order-independent connections to InterfaceListManager",
  "description": "The InterfaceFrame and its InterfaceTreeModel both connect to the\nInterfaceListManager's interfaceListChanged. The InterfaceFrame's\nresetInterfaceTreeDisplay must be called when the interface list is\nchanged, but it must be called *after* the InterfaceTreeModel is\nreset, so that the values for proxy_model_.rowCount() have updated.\nIt must be called when the model is reset for any reason, for that\nmatter, not just from an interface list changed event.\nThe QTreeView is already automatically connected to the modelReset,\nbut not some of the other tests in resetInterfaceTreeDisplay.\n\nThis happens to work in the current setup, but is an artifact of\nexactly when the connections are made. Properly connect\nresetInterfaceTreeDisplay to the model being reset instead of\ncalling it in InterfaceFrame's interfaceListChanged. Also connect\nthe updateSelectedInterfaces to modelReset for the same reason.",
  "state": "merged",
